#: NAVIGATION.md:1
msgid ""
"Multiple Walkers Metadynamics Simulations with a Reactive Machine Learning "
"Interatomic Potential"
msgstr ""
"Reactive Machine Learning Interatomic Potential を用いた Multiple Walkers "
"Metadynamics シミュレーション"

#: NAVIGATION.md:3
msgid ""
"In molecular dynamics (MD) simulations, different kinds of empirical "
"interatomic potentials have been used to study various problems. However, "
"those empirical potentials are usually incapable of describing chemical "
"reactions as they need a proper description of the formation and breakage of"
" chemical bonds. On the other hand, interatomic potentials derived from "
"first-principles methods (e.g., density functional theory) are often "
"expensive and can only be applied to small systems. For a more extensive "
"system, such as chemical reactions in a bulk solution with explicit solvent "
"molecules, the timescale of the process is often too long for first-"
"principles MD simulations to reach. Recently, reactive machine learning "
"interatomic potentials (MLIP) have been of great interest to the community "
"as they can provide atomistic details to a system of interest with first-"
"principles insights and a speed comparable to empirical potentials. They can"
" be combined with various enhanced sampling techniques (e.g., umbrella "
"sampling, metadynamics, etc.) to more efficiently explore the free energy "
"space of a chemical reaction."
msgstr ""
"Molecular Dynamics（MD）では、さまざまな問題を調べるために各種の Empirical Interatomic Potentials "
"が使われてきた。しかし、化学反応には Chemical Bonds の形成と切断の適切な記述が必要なため、これらの Potentials "
"では通常扱えない。一方、Density Functional Theory などの First-principles 手法から得る "
"Interatomic Potentials は計算コストが高く、小さな系にしか適用できないことが多い。明示的な溶媒分子を含む Bulk "
"Solution 中の化学反応のような大きな系では、過程の Time Scale が First-principles MD "
"で到達するには長すぎることが多い。近年は、First-principles の知見と、Empirical Potentials "
"に匹敵する速度で原子レベルの詳細を与えられる Reactive Machine Learning Interatomic "
"Potentials（MLIP）が注目されている。Umbrella Sampling や Metadynamics などの Enhanced "
"Sampling と組み合わせれば、化学反応の自由エネルギー空間をさらに効率よく探索できる。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:5
msgid ""
"This tutorial uses Atomic Simulation Environment (ASE) to perform multiple "
"walkers metadynamics simulations with a trained equivariant message-passing "
"neural network potential, MACE, to explore the free energy surface of "
"nitrate anion dissociation at its triplet state in an aqueous solution. In "
"principle, multiple walkers metadynamics can be more efficient than standard"
" metadynamics when the free energy surface of interest has more than two "
"local minima. This tutorial uses MACE as the MLIP of choice, but different "
"MLIPs can be used in ASE without additional compilation if the ASE "
"calculator for that particular MLIP is available in the version used."
msgstr ""
"このチュートリアルでは、Atomic Simulation Environment（ASE）と、学習済みの Equivariant Message-"
"passing Neural Network Potential である MACE を用いて Multiple Walkers Metadynamics"
" を実行する。対象は、水溶液中の Triplet State にある Nitrate Anion の Dissociation "
"の自由エネルギー面である。原理的には、対象の自由エネルギー面に Local Minima が3つ以上ある場合、Multiple Walkers "
"Metadynamics は通常の Metadynamics より効率よくなる可能性がある。ここでは MLIP に MACE を選ぶが、使用する ASE"
" に対応する Calculator があれば、追加のコンパイルなしで他の MLIPs も利用できる。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:7
msgid ""
"Depending on your previous exposure and interest in the topics, you may want"
" to look at the lessons on PLUMED syntax, metadynamics, and external "
"tutorials on training a MACE potential by its developer group."
msgstr ""
"これまでの経験や関心に応じて、PLUMED の構文、Metadynamics のレッスン、または MACE 開発グループによる Potential "
"学習の外部チュートリアルを参照するとよい。"

